+// Harvest Moon: Animal Parade mod "romance_any_gender", part two: the adoption. (Part one, who can
+// fall in love with the player, is romance_any_gender.cpp.)
+//
+// In the original game a couple's first child comes in two of the spouse's events: L000015, at
+// bedtime, where the spouse asks whether the player wants a child and whether a boy or a girl, and
+// days later L000016, the birth. The second child repeats it with L000029 and L000030. (Each
+// candidate has their own copy of these events: GIL_L000015 is Gill's event 1811, for example;
+// event/varSet_love*.db gives each event its character and its messages.)
+//
+// For a couple of the same sex, the mod plays new scenes instead of these four. In place of
+// L000015 and L000029 the spouse asks the same questions with their own lines and the couple
+// wishes for a baby; the question is marked done as in the game, so the game's own wait for the
+// birth starts. Days later, in place of L000016 and L000030, the Harvest Goddess appears in the
+// house and gives them a baby to adopt, for their great love, and the scene ends the way the
+// birth does (the baby's name, what the baby will be like, the parenting book).
+//
+// How it is done:
+// - The scene an event plays comes from a table at 0x80485160, 12 bytes per event: {kind, file,
+//   message files}. 0x801320B4 (event in r3) returns the file, a number in the game's file table
+//   at 0x80431340 (16 bytes per file, a pointer to its name first). The mod wraps 0x801320B4: for
+//   a same-sex couple's L000015, L000016, L000029 or L000030 it answers with one of the disc's
+//   unused test scenes in script/test/sample/ (sample_125 and sample_126 the questions,
+//   sample_127, sample_122 and sample_123 the Goddess), and the mod's copies of those hold the
+//   new scenes.
+// - The scene is OPAL bytecode built here (OpalScene below); tools/game_files.py describes the
+//   format. The commands are the ones the game's own scenes use for the same things: the bedtime
+//   talk is staged like loveCommon/LC_L000015.opb, the Goddess like the Harvest Goddess's own
+//   baby scene (loveGdss/GDSS_L000016.opb), and the end does what the birth scenes do
+//   (loveGirl/LG_L000016.opb and loveBoy/LB_L000016.opb).
+// - The spouse's lines are their own: an event's messages are 32 slots, -320 to -289, filled from
+//   its message set (event/msgSet_love*.db). The questions use their sets, the Goddess's scenes
+//   the births' (the baby's name, what the baby will be like, good night and the book). The
+//   preview plays both halves as the question, so the mod's copy of the sets file adds those ten
+//   birth lines to the question sets too, as slots 20 to 29. The Goddess's lines are new: the mod adds them to
+//   every love message pack (msglang/<language>/<male|female>/love*.mpc) as messages 0xE000 and
+//   on, in Spanish for the Spanish packs and in English for the others.
+// - The Harvest Goddess and the Harvest King as spouses keep their own scenes: their child already
+//   comes by magic.
+//
+// The wedding (each candidate's L000007) keeps the original scene but for its last shot: there
+// the groom carries the bride in his arms (motion 0x225 for both, placed on the same spot), and two
+// brides or two grooms end up inside each other. For a same-sex couple the wedding plays a copy
+// (sample_120.opb for two brides, sample_121.opb for two grooms) where that shot has them side by
+// side, cheering.
+
